Cases written with the rule (2026-11-09), not drawn from a labeling round.
An invented author whose change descriptions hold lists of uneven items that
open on different words. The author sections build the voice; a text is held
to that author's own range of item length, item openers and sentence openers.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(cache): keep the key stable

Two workers raced on the key, and the loser wrote a stale entry.

- Sorted the inputs before hashing.
- The lock now covers the read as well as the write, which closes the window where a second worker could see half an entry.
- Tests.
- I left the old key format readable for one release so nobody has to wipe their cache by hand.
-- author/change-description whole --
feat(cli): read the token from the environment

People kept pasting tokens into the config file and then committing it by accident.

- The CLI checks the flag, then the environment, then the config file.
- Docs for all three.
- If the config file holds a token, it prints a warning that names the file and the line.
- Removed the old prompt.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(parser): accept tabs in the config file

A user pasted a snippet from the docs and got an error about line two that made no sense.

- Tabs and spaces both count as indentation now.
- Mixed indentation in one block is still an error, but the message says which lines disagree.
- New test file.
- The docs snippet used tabs, so I changed it to spaces anyway.
-- author/change-description whole --
perf(build): run lint and tests in parallel

A full CI run took about nine minutes, and most of it was waiting.

- Lint, tests and the type check run side by side.
- Caching the module download saves another minute on a cold runner.
- I kept the deploy step serial on purpose since it touches shared state.
- Timings are in the PR comments.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(upload): pick up where a dropped link left off

Big uploads over slow links failed and started over from zero.

- The code to pick up where it left off was there all along; a typo in the offset check meant it never ran.
- Added a test that drops the link halfway.
- Progress shows the offset it restarted from now.
- Nothing changes for small files.
-- author/change-description whole --
docs: rewrite the setup guide

I tried the guide fresh on three machines and hit a different wall on each one.

- macOS needed one more package than the guide said.
- Linux was fine.
- The Windows steps were missing a whole section about long paths, which is why the build failed with a confusing error about a missing file that was right there.
- Screenshots are gone; they went stale every release.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(invoice): count refunds once

A refund issued on the same day as the charge was counted twice in the totals.

- Totals read refunds from the ledger instead of the order.
- Discounts and taxes were already right, so I left them alone.
- One migration fixes the three invoices this hit.
- Test.
-- author/change-description whole --
feat(search): remember filters

Coming back to the search page after lunch meant setting everything up again.

- Filters, sort order and the last query are kept per user.
- They clear when you sign out.
- I stored them in local storage rather than the server because nobody asked to share them across devices.
- A reset button.
-- author/change-description whole --
chore: pin the toolchain

CI and laptops disagreed about formatting about once a week.

- The compiler, linter and formatter versions live in one file.
- The bootstrap script reads it.
- Anyone on an older formatter gets one big diff the first time; after that it settles.
- Renovate bumps the file.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(backup): check space before starting

The nightly backup failed halfway when the disk filled and left a partial archive.

- It checks free space, file count and a checksum first.
- A partial archive from an earlier failure is deleted on the next run instead of being kept forever.
- Alerts name the host.
- I did not touch the restore path.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(menu): stop the footer covering the menu on phones

Below about four hundred pixels the footer slid over the menu, which is most phones held upright.

- The footer is in the page flow again instead of fixed.
- Search moved into the menu on small screens.
- I checked it on two phones and the simulator.
- No change on desktop.
-- author/change-description whole --
feat(health): report each dependency

Ops wanted to know which dependency was down without reading logs at three in the morning.

- The health check reports the database, the queue and the cache on their own lines.
- A slow dependency shows its latency.
- The overall status is the worst of the three.
- Dashboards read the new fields; the old single field stays for a release.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(sync): skip hidden and lock files

One user lost an editor swap file when the sync deleted it on the other machine.

- Hidden files, lock files and temp files are never synced.
- The ignore list is in the settings if someone really wants one of them.
- Test for each pattern.
- I wrote to the user who reported it.
-- author/change-description whole --
chore(email): shorten the account emails

People told us they skimmed past the long versions anyway.

- Welcome, reset and invite emails are a few lines each.
- The reset link expires in an hour, and the email says so.
- Plain text versions match the HTML ones now; they had drifted.
- Legal footer unchanged.
-- author/change-description whole --
refactor(telemetry): one interface for logs and metrics

Swapping the vendor would have meant touching about forty files.

- Logging, metrics and tracing sit behind one small interface.
- The vendor adapter is one file.
- Nothing calls the vendor library directly any more; a lint rule keeps it that way.
- Behavior is the same, so no changelog entry.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(dates): parse two-digit years

A user in Sydney sent a really clear example of a date that came out a century off.

- Two-digit years read as this century unless that lands more than ten years ahead.
- Time zones are applied before the day is picked, which fixes the off-by-one near midnight.
- Leap years had a test already; it was just wrong.
- Changelog entry.
-- author/change-description whole --
feat(import): read JSON lines

The importer only took CSV, and two teams were converting by hand every week.

- CSV, TSV and JSON lines all go through one reader.
- I left Excel out on purpose because the library pulls in far too much for one format.
- A bad line names its number.
- Examples in the docs.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(retry): give up on errors that will not pass

The client retried every error five times, which hid real bugs behind a slow failure.

- Timeouts and resets retry.
- So does the one server error that means try again later.
- Everything else fails right away with the server's message.
- The retry count is in the config if someone needs more.
-- author/change-description whole --
feat(dashboard): split build time from queue time

When the total grew it was hard to tell whether builds got slower or we just waited longer.

- Build, test and queue time sit side by side.
- Each one has its own trend line for the last thirty days.
- The total is still there at the top.
- I did not add alerts yet; that wants its own discussion.
-- author/change-description whole --
fix(errors): name the path in file errors

Missing files, bad permissions and full disks all printed the same vague message.

- Each error names the path and the operation.
- A permission error says which user the process runs as.
- A full disk says how much space it needed.
- Tests for all three, using a small fake filesystem.
-- author/change-description whole --
chore(deps): drop the legacy importer

Nothing has called the old importer since the new one shipped in the spring.

- Removed the code, its tests and its docs page.
- The docs page was confusing people, which is really why I did this now.
- One config key it read is gone; loading a config that sets it prints a note.
- The binary is about two megabytes smaller.
-- author/change-description whole --
feat(cli): add a dry run

I wanted this while testing the migration and figured others would too.

- The dry run prints the plan, the files it would touch and the commands it would run.
- Nothing is written.
- Exit code is the same as a real run would give, so scripts can use it as a check.
- It is a flag, not a subcommand.
-- hit/change-description whole --
fix(parser): read the new header

Updated the parser to read the new header.

- Updated the parser to read the new header format.
- Updated the writer to emit the new header format.
- Updated the loader to accept the new header format.
- Updated the tests to cover the new header format.
- Updated the docs to describe the new header format.
- Updated the cache to store the new header format.
- Updated the index to track the new header format.
- Updated the server to serve the new header format.
- Updated the client to request the new header format.
- Updated the config to name the new header format.
- Updated the logger to print the new header format.
- Updated the router to route the new header format.
- Updated the importer to read the new header format.
- Updated the exporter to write the new header format.
- Updated the checker to verify the new header format.
- Updated the viewer to show the new header format.
- Updated the archive to keep the new header format.
- Updated the backup to copy the new header format.
- Updated the mirror to sync the new header format.
- Updated the guide to explain the new header format.
- Updated the schema to declare the new header format.
- Updated the fixtures to use the new header format.
-- pass/change-description whole --
fix(parser): read the new header

The parser reads the new header now, which unblocks the 2.3 release.

- Rewrote the parser.
- The writer kept its old header until the 2.3 release, so readers built before then still open the files it writes.
- Tests for the empty file and the file with no trailing newline.
- Moved the loader into its own package after the cache split.
- Docs.
- I left the old reader in place for one release, since two teams still ship files from the old writer.
- Cache keys include the header version now.
- The importer was the hard part: it guessed the header from the first line, and a file that opened on a comment fooled it every time.
- Benchmarks.
- A user in Sydney sent the file that showed the bug, which made the fix a lot faster to find.
- Moved the fixtures.
- The schema names both versions, and the checker reports which one a file uses when it rejects it.
- Smaller error messages.
- The viewer shows the header version in the status bar now, after a request on the tracker last month.
- Changelog entry.
